INT. NEW BEGINNINGS FERTILITY CLINIC - WAITING ROOM - DAY

Soft jazz. Beige everything. A fish tank with one very depressed fish. Applause-ready bright. A wall of baby photos.

Behind the front desk, BRENDA OKONKWO, 50s, receptionist, queen of the clipboard. At the coffee machine, DR. ELLIOT VANCE, 40s, handsome in a way that costs money. On the couch, MARA FELDMAN, 30s, nervous, holding a stack of forms, and next to her, her husband BRAD FELDMAN, 30s, who doesn't look up from his phone.

Enter BRETT FELDMAN, 30s, in a suit that doesn't fit, with a bouquet.

BRETT
Honey! I came as soon as I could!

Everyone turns. Brad looks up. Mara looks at Brad. Brad looks at Brett. Brett looks at the bouquet, then at Mara.

BRENDA
(deadpan)
Well. That's a lot of husbands.

MARA
Brett is Brad's brother.

BRETT
I'm the fun one.

BRAD
He is not the fun one.

DR. VANCE
(reading a clipboard)
Mrs. Feldman? We're ready for you.

MARA
Both of them can come?

DR. VANCE
(smiling too widely)
Of course. The more the merrier.

Mara stands. Brad stands. Brett stands. They all move toward the door, then all stop, because Brenda is holding up a hand.

BRENDA
Just the one husband, hon.

BRAD
I'll go.

BRETT
I'll go.

MARA
I'm going. Alone.

DR. VANCE
(brightly)
Excellent.

Mara exits through the inner door. Dr. Vance follows. It closes. Brad and Brett stand in silence. The fish blows a bubble.

BRAD
Why are you here?

BRETT
Mom said you needed support.

BRAD
Mom said that?

BRETT
She said you looked "fragile."

BRENDA
(not looking up)
He does.

ON PHONE: Brad's screen lights. A text from an unknown number.

ON PHONE: "dont let him in the room. hes not who u think."

BRAD
(reading, pale)
Oh.

BRETT
What?

BRAD
Nothing. Spam.

BRETT
Let me see.

BRAD
No.

BRETT
Brad.

They grapple for the phone, Brett lunges, Brad ducks, the bouquet goes flying and lands in the fish tank. The fish, for the first time, looks interested.

BRENDA
(sighs)
That's a four-hundred-dollar fish.

INT. NEW BEGINNINGS FERTILITY CLINIC - EXAM ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Mara on the table, paper gown. Dr. Vance snaps on gloves, humming. On the counter, a vial with a handwritten label. She squints at it.

MARA
That says Feldman.

DR. VANCE
It does.

MARA
Which Feldman?

DR. VANCE
(gently)
The one who's paying.

A pause. Mara sits up.

MARA
Doctor, which one is it?

DR. VANCE
(his smile never moves)
Does it matter?

The lights flicker. Out in the waiting room, the fish tank bubbles. Brenda, alone at her desk, quietly locks the front door.

This is the last time anyone will ask that question.

Brad and Brett burst through the inner door, panting, the soggy bouquet still in Brett's hand.

BRAD
Mara, don't let him

BRETT
Honey, it's not what

DR. VANCE
(overlapping)
Gentlemen, please, this is a sterile environment.

MARA
(overlapping)
Which of you?

BRAD
(overlapping)
It wasn't me!

BRETT
(overlapping)
It was supposed to be a gift!

Mara looks at one, then the other, then at the vial, then at Dr. Vance, who has quietly slipped a hand into his coat pocket. A cold gleam of metal.

DR. VANCE
Everyone stay very calm.

BRENDA (O.S.)
(through the door)
Doctor, your two o'clock is here!

DR. VANCE
(without turning)
Reschedule her.

BRENDA (O.S.)
She says she's the police.

Everyone freezes. Dr. Vance's smile finally falls off his face. Brett holds up the soggy bouquet like a white flag.

BRETT
(whispering)
Can I go now?
